{
  "dom_id": "step-140701",
  "name": "Introduction",
  "problem": "Let's think about how to graph the solutions to the following two-variable inequality:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/9c366bd1e6e436a908877b903d309078b7a40320a279065ffe795b52eece4a8b.svg) \n\nSince this is a two-variable inequality, we must represent its solutions in the ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/39303ee53d6cd0a654e183557bb493fd0ba5b887f96f5d7d871a9be772ce1808.svg)-plane. \n\nWe start by replacing the inequality symbol ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/790374cc61ee8a73065b09d2bc1bfbb37ac255dcac47e7784962c63057025fff.svg) with an equals sign ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/0390f8b1f8405fa7ec0dd6ce7af3bccd7e0474a8ed59e323595062ced4c42fcf.svg) and plot the resulting line. In this case, we get the line ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/0959b88bad14750ae0ac71cfc63edbe90a03ae64db7fc0cb56cbf827289f11d5.svg)\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/3497eb8d3f071794cd899c5c62a88500fbcf7b69a34d58171866a078a185bfc9.png)\n\nNotice that we have a \"*greater than*\" ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/790374cc61ee8a73065b09d2bc1bfbb37ac255dcac47e7784962c63057025fff.svg) inequality. Therefore, we draw a *dashed* line to denote that points on the line are *not* solutions to our inequality.\n\nNow, since we're solving ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/0d93a37b8a2c41f9bfbef6f40271c3a43ae9246dc55b76c6154ddb2a3305f98f.svg) we need to shade all points whose ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg)-value is *greater than* its ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/fcc5df999e3b49fae1685ee0ab5bd03709804e1dd49f2ee722c4269eb0f5506d.svg)-value. This is given by all of the points that lie *above* our dashed line. So, let's shade these in.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/3c1df1de40b9ccb8ea9893a0c45ef3072e0380f0a3683d4f7d690e771d0ff852.png)\n\nAnd we're done! All of the points in the shaded region satisfy the inequality ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/f55852c049661527d11683dc61ede4846eae70f51ce317220d7fea47cea44823.svg)",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
